# VPN settings for docker-compose.vpn.yml. Copy to `vpn.env` (git-ignored) and
# fill in ONE of the blocks below. These are gluetun's own variables; its wiki
# lists every option and provider:
# https://github.com/qdm12/gluetun-wiki/tree/main/setup/providers
#
# Pick a provider that ALLOWS peer-to-peer traffic (many free tiers do not).
# Port forwarding makes peer-to-peer much faster; see "Port forwarding" below.
# → docs/acquisition-egress-vpn.md

# --- A) A supported provider (Mullvad, ProtonVPN, AirVPN, IVPN, PIA, …) ---------
# Get the WireGuard private key and address from your provider's
# "WireGuard configuration" page.
VPN_SERVICE_PROVIDER=mullvad
VPN_TYPE=wireguard
WIREGUARD_PRIVATE_KEY=
WIREGUARD_ADDRESSES=
# Optional: where to exit
# SERVER_COUNTRIES=Netherlands

# --- B) Any other WireGuard server (paste the values from its .conf file) ------
# VPN_SERVICE_PROVIDER=custom
# VPN_TYPE=wireguard
# WIREGUARD_ENDPOINT_IP=        # an IP address; gluetun does not accept a hostname here
# WIREGUARD_ENDPOINT_PORT=51820
# WIREGUARD_PUBLIC_KEY=         # the [Peer] PublicKey
# WIREGUARD_PRIVATE_KEY=        # the [Interface] PrivateKey
# WIREGUARD_PRESHARED_KEY=      # only if the .conf has one
# WIREGUARD_ADDRESSES=          # the [Interface] Address

# --- Port forwarding (optional) -------------------------------------------------
# Lets peers connect IN, not only out. slskd listens for peers on 50300.
# If your provider gives you a fixed forwarded port, forward 50300 there and open
# it on the tunnel:
# FIREWALL_VPN_INPUT_PORTS=50300
# Providers with automatic, changing ports (ProtonVPN, PIA): VPN_PORT_FORWARDING=on
# opens a random port, which slskd does not follow yet, so it only helps clients
# that do.
